      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "1. Recommendations and decisions concerning treatment should primarily be based on the absolute evaluation of risk and risk reduction and not on calculation of a relative risk situation. 2. The therapeutic benefit in women at low risk should be balanced against possible physical and psychic side effects and submitted to a cost/benefit analysis. 3. The fact that coronary heart disease is rare in young women must not at all be reason for a less consequent treatment and prevention in women with established coronary heart disease."},
